**Rotting attribution comments in production code will mislead future readers**

Comments like `// anthropicreviewbot (PR #69): ...` and `// anthropicreviewbot (PR #69, round 2): ...` embed reviewer identity and PR number directly in production source. These will be false/misleading context the moment the PR merges (PR #69 will be closed, the reviewer identity is external noise). The explanatory rationale in these comments is valuable — the attribution wrapper is not. Strip the attribution prefix and keep only the technical explanation.

*Suggested fix:*

```suggestion
// Validate maxReviews: values < 1 trip on the very first post
	// with no signal the config is nonsensical, silently defeating the guard.
	// Number.isFinite also catches NaN: every `< 1` and `>= maxReviews`
	// comparison against NaN is false, so an unvalidated NaN disables the
	// breaker just as silently as maxReviews: 0 does.
```

