**Attribution comments in test file embed PR number and round — will rot immediately**

Lines like `// anthropicreviewbot (PR #69, round 2):` and `// anthropicreviewbot (PR #69, round 3):` in `src/watch.test.ts` embed reviewer identity, PR number, and review round. These will be meaningless to any future reader who doesn't have this PR open, and will actively mislead anyone who needs to understand why the test exists. The prior review already flagged this and it remains unaddressed across multiple rounds. Replace with plain rationale comments explaining the defect being guarded against, without reviewer/PR attribution.

*Suggested fix:*

```suggestion
// NaN guard: `NaN < 1` is false, so without Number.isFinite the original
// `< 1` check let a non-finite maxReviews silently through —
// and every `recentPosts.length >= NaN` comparison is also false, so
// the breaker would then never trip, defeating it silently.
```

